WEBVTT

NOTE On-screen visual text only; this approved video has no audio track.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.350
Without an external record, remembering a quantity depends on one person’s memory.

2
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:14.200
Seven objects can be represented by seven persistent marks.

3
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:21.550
The record preserves the quantity after the objects are out of sight.

4
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:28.900
Twenty-four marks represent the same quantity as the symbols two and four.

5
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:35.750
Positional notation organizes it as two tens and four units.

6
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:43.100
A shorter record is easier to manipulate only when the convention is understood.

7
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:50.450
A fixed operation always transforms the input in the same way.

8
00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:57.300
Separating the program lets the same mechanism perform addition or multiplication.

9
00:00:57.300 --> 00:01:04.967
The machine becomes reusable because the procedure is no longer tied to its physical structure.

10
00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:12.317
A learning program receives examples and a measurable objective.

11
00:01:12.317 --> 00:01:19.167
Prediction error changes its internal parameters.

12
00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:27.217
The resulting transformation depends on data; learning is not writing every rule manually.

13
00:01:27.717 --> 00:01:34.567
Four independent products can be computed one after another.

14
00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:41.417
Two compute units can share those products without waiting on independent operations.

15
00:01:41.417 --> 00:01:48.767
The improvement depends on dependencies, memory and communication, not only on unit count.

16
00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:56.117
Representation, programming, learning and scaling solve different constraints.

17
00:01:56.117 --> 00:02:02.967
A modern system still needs symbols, programs and physical resources.

18
00:02:02.967 --> 00:02:10.317
This history explains technical dependencies; it does not make AGI inevitable.

